WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.015 --> 00:00:15.517
wanted to return to the prince's room and eat nuts.

2
00:00:17.198 --> 00:00:19.300
But first he had to deal with his itchy nose.

3
00:00:20.742 --> 00:00:22.363
So he continued to sit at the table.

4
00:00:24.245 --> 00:00:27.828
He wrinkled his nose, trying to get rid of the annoying sensation.

5
00:00:29.108 --> 00:00:31.049
But that only made him want to sneeze.

6
00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:37.872
As Tom's eyes began to water, his distress became obvious to everyone in the room.

7
00:00:37.892 --> 00:00:41.874
"Do you need some assistance, sir?"

8
00:00:42.314 --> 00:00:43.714
the royal taster asked.

9
00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:46.556
"Was there something wrong with the food?"

10
00:00:48.937 --> 00:00:52.278
"There was nothing wrong with the food," the head chef snapped.

11
00:00:52.298 --> 00:00:56.620
"I sampled all the dishes myself before they were brought to the table.

12
00:00:58.096 --> 00:00:59.758
Everything was delicious!"

13
00:00:59.778 --> 00:01:03.981
"Perhaps you need more water?"

14
00:01:05.502 --> 00:01:07.684
The royal cupbearer filled Tom's cup again.

15
00:01:09.866 --> 00:01:11.928
Tom needed to do something right now!

16
00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:15.731
He beckoned for Lord Hertford to approach the table.

17
00:01:15.751 --> 00:01:19.034
"What's the matter, Your Highness?"

18
00:01:20.335 --> 00:01:22.457
Lord Hertford's face was full of concern.

19
00:01:22.477 --> 00:01:26.100
"My nose itches terribly.

20
00:01:27.272 --> 00:01:30.975
I have so many servants that there has to be one in charge of my nose.

21
00:01:32.576 --> 00:01:35.559
Please summon the royal nose scratcher immediately."

22
00:01:35.579 --> 00:01:42.945
"I'm sorry, sir, but there is no royal nose scratcher," Lord Hertford said.

23
00:01:42.965 --> 00:01:46.668
"No royal nose scratcher?"

24
00:01:47.428 --> 00:01:49.810
By now the tears were streaming down Tom's face.

25
00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:52.593
"Then what am I supposed to do?"

26
00:01:54.975 --> 00:01:56.416
Lord Hertford was baffled.

27
00:01:57.656 --> 00:02:01.719
"Surely this isn't the first time in your life that your nose has itched.

28
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.601
What have you done in the past?"

29
00:02:04.621 --> 00:02:11.506
"When I was on Offal Tom remembered the king's orders.

30
00:02:11.526 --> 00:02:14.828
"Oh, I don't care what the proper thing is.

31
00:02:14.848 --> 00:02:17.950
I need to scratch my own nose!"

32
00:02:19.811 --> 00:02:21.453
And that's exactly what he did.

33
00:02:24.595 --> 00:02:26.216
No one gasped or laughed.

34
00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.042
Lord Hertford was just relieved that Tom hadn't said anything more about Offal Street.

35
00:02:33.242 --> 00:02:38.145
"Very good, Your Highness," Lord Hertford said, and the servants broke into applause.

36
00:02:41.926 --> 00:02:45.788
The royal napkin holder arrived with a gold bowl filled with rose water.

37
00:02:47.249 --> 00:02:49.049
Over his arm he carried a napkin.

38
00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:54.592
Tom was supposed to wash and dry his hands after meals, but he didn't know that.

39
00:02:56.332 --> 00:02:59.474
He raised the dish to his lips and solemnly took a drink.

40
00:03:01.294 --> 00:03:02.915
"It doesn't have much flavor."

41
00:03:04.336 --> 00:03:06.937
Tom handed the bowl back to the royal napkin holder.

42
00:03:06.957 --> 00:03:11.399
"Please make it stronger next time," he said to the head chef.

43
00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.422
She started to protest, but Tom stood up, which signaled that lunch was over.

44
00:03:18.923 --> 00:03:21.464
Tom announced that he wanted to return to his room.

45
00:03:25.504 --> 00:03:28.886
"I'd like to be left alone for the rest of the afternoon," he said.

46
00:03:31.428 --> 00:03:34.950
As soon as his door closed, Tom began hunting for a nutcracker.

47
00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:40.833
"Prince Edward has everything, so he must have a nutcracker."

48
00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:46.897
But before he found one, he was distracted by shelves full of books.

49
00:03:49.018 --> 00:03:51.080
One book was about castles and forts.

50
00:03:52.508 --> 00:03:55.369
Another was about famous kings and queens of the past.

51
00:03:55.389 --> 00:04:00.070
"Father Andrew would like that," Tom thought.

52
00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:05.752
"There are so many books here that I don't know where to start reading!"

53
00:04:07.532 --> 00:04:12.374
Just then he noticed Royal Court Etiquette: A Guide for the Young Prince.

54
00:04:14.514 --> 00:04:16.775
"That would be useful," Tom thought.

55
00:04:18.715 --> 00:04:20.656
He opened the book and turned the pages.

56
00:04:22.076 --> 00:04:26.679
The book covered everything from when to wear a crown to who should bow to whom.

57
00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.262
There was even a whole chapter on table settings.

58
00:04:31.282 --> 00:04:35.765
"Who knew there were so many types of silverware?"

59
00:04:37.346 --> 00:04:42.170
Tom pored over the illustrations of dessert spoons, salad forks, and steak knives.

60
00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:46.753
"I guess I should stop using my hands to eat."

61
00:04:49.674 --> 00:04:53.962
Tom soon grew bored with this chapter and turned to the section on armor.

62
00:04:56.163 --> 00:04:58.665
He took the book over to the prince's armor to compare it.

63
00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:05.930
Made of metal and covered with gold designs, Prince Edward's armor was beautiful to look at.

64
00:05:07.552 --> 00:05:09.673
But Tom wanted to do more than look at it.

65
00:05:10.954 --> 00:05:12.515
He wanted to try it on.

66
00:05:12.535 --> 00:05:18.660
"Prince Edward and I are the same size, so I know it'll fit me," he thought.

67
00:05:20.024 --> 00:05:22.486
"But I don't think I can get into it without help."

68
00:05:25.588 --> 00:05:29.051
Then he noticed the helmet and armor-covered gloves on a table.

69
00:05:31.432 --> 00:05:34.555
As Tom picked up a glove, a heavy metal disk fell out.

70
00:05:34.575 --> 00:05:38.538
"Well, that thing isn't mentioned in the book!"

71
00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.980
Tom watched the disk roll across the floor.

72
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.704
"But it'll be perfect for cracking nuts."

73
00:05:49.632 --> 00:05:52.314
Tom left the disk on the floor while he put on the gloves.

74
00:05:55.795 --> 00:05:58.937
Then he put on the helmet and found his way to the mirror.

75
00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:05.601
It was hard to see through the slits for his eyes.

76
00:06:05.621 --> 00:06:12.064
"Phew! This helmet is much heavier and hotter than I expected," Tom thought.

77
00:06:12.084 --> 00:06:14.906
"I need to take it off."

78
00:06:16.507 --> 00:06:21.328
He tried to yank off the helmet, but "Ahh!"

79
00:06:21.869 --> 00:06:23.213
It was stuck on his head!
